<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Nightingale returns for her six-month review. The extra half hour of work agreed in June held without post-exertional malaise, and she later added another half hour, so she now works four to five hours a day in 45-minute blocks with rests between. Her July cold caused a flare that settled in about ten days on her flare plan, with no fever afterward and no night sweats or back or joint pain. Since then she has had no crash. She goes out twice a week, for a short walk or a meeting, and plans a rest day after each outing. She is lightheaded on standing about twice a week. Sleep is still not fully refreshing, and acetaminophen is needed a few times a month. She takes cholecalciferol daily. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>One flare after a cold in July; no crash since</td></tr><tr><td>Energy management</td><td>Four to five hours of work a day in 45-minute blocks</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Out of the house twice a week with a rest day after</td></tr><tr><td>Orthostatic symptoms</td><td>About twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Infection warning signs</td><td>No fever, night sweats, or back or joint pain since the cold</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
