    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">ME/CFS, moderate, improving (G93.32)</content>. Stable on her energy management plan with more working time and no crash since the July flare. PROMIS fatigue 64 (from 71 at intake) and physical function 38 (from 32); pain score 3. Orthostatic intolerance has improved on the standing test. [S]<list><item>Continue the energy management plan; any further increase only in small steps she chooses, guided by the diary.</item><item>Continue fluids, salt, and compression.</item><item>Next care plan review in about three months, and at least yearly after that.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Vitamin D deficiency, replete (E55.9)</content>. 25-hydroxyvitamin D 34 ng/mL. [S]<list><item>Continue cholecalciferol 2,000 units daily.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D after starting repletion</td><td>Once, about three months after starting</td><td>Completed today</td><td>34 ng/mL, now replete; drawn today after it was missed at the three-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 and GAD-7</td><td>At diagnosis and at each review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 5 with item 9 scored 0; GAD-7 4</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PROMIS fatigue and physical function T-scores, pain score</td><td>At diagnosis and at each review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fatigue 64, physical function 38, pain 3</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Ten-minute standing test</td><td>Repeat at six months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Heart rate rise of 18/min, down from 26/min</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptom review, including infection warning signs</td><td>Every review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No crash since the July flare; no fever, night sweats, or focal pain</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Energy management and flare plan review</td><td>Every review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Flare plan worked as intended during the July cold</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review</td><td>Every review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cholecalciferol daily; acetaminophen a few times a month</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>ME/CFS specialist team</td><td>At diagnosis (NICE 1.4.3)</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Still no regional service; care continues in primary care with the occupational therapist available as needed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Agree an energy management plan with a stable baseline and no more than one crash a month by the six-month review. Outcome by 1858-09-14: One flare in three months, after a cold; no crash from overexertion since the summer [S]</item><item>Keep working within her energy limits, aiming for four hours a day in planned blocks by the six-month review. Outcome by 1858-09-14: Working four to five hours a day in 45-minute blocks with rest between [S]</item><item>Fewer orthostatic symptoms with fluids, salt, compression, and seated or reclined tasks by the three-month review. Outcome by 1858-06-01: Lightheaded on standing two or three times a week instead of daily [S]</item><item>Replete vitamin D to 30 ng/mL or higher. Outcome by 1858-09-14: 25-hydroxyvitamin D 34 ng/mL [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Myalgic encephalomyelitis (or encephalopathy)/chronic fatigue syndrome: diagnosis and management (NICE guideline NG206) (2021); Diagnosing ME/CFS (2024); Grach SL, et al. Diagnosis and Management of Myalgic Encephalomyelitis/Chronic Fatigue Syndrome. Mayo Clin Proc 2023;98(10):1544-1551 (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Adult preventive visit next month. ME/CFS review in about three months, then at least yearly. Next scheduled visit 1858-10-12: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
